125
00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.000
week two, why we play like apes. The readings

126
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.580
are the prologue and chapter one of Fox's book the ball, plus

127
00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.920
Connor's chapter on play, social learning,

128
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:46.320
and teaching, plus the lecture slides. Here's Fox's argument in

129
00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.380
one sentence. Play looks pointless,

130
00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.160
it costs real energy, and it can get you killed. Which means

131
00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.720
evolution kept it for a reason. It builds

132
00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.700
brains, it builds bodies, and it builds the ability to agree on

133
00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.060
